codex
I found two concrete precision differences. HF stores its recurrent cache in BF16, while this decoder keeps it in FP32. Separately, the fused kernel stores FP32 buffers but defaults to TF32 unpacking, which reduces precision on values reused each token. I’m checking which paths lose precision and which could explain the long-context result before ranking them in the report.

